From 9be7a87be18eecb383f44d1d84cb98ac561efd5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 23:18:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 93/93] ipa: soft: Add a noise reduction algorithm

Denoise sets the GPU debayer's noise filter for each frame from the vendor
tuning's adaptive Bayer filter, by the frame's gain: the noise model (the
variance of the 12-bit signal is the region's noise times its level over 64,
which on this sensor measures within 15% of its raw frames) and the filter
strengths for red/blue and green between the anchors' levels, as the kernel
width, the inverse of the strength (smaller is stronger). The regions blend
across the gaps between their gain ranges.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
